        sisterModels: [ { name: "BMW 540i (E39)", note: "The legendary E39 540i utilized the exact same M62B44 engine, earning immense praise for its silky power delivery, but suffering from the exact same devastating timing chain guide failures." } ],
        tuningPotential: [
          { stage: "Stage 1 (Software Tune)", power: "300 - 315 hp", notes: "A software flash optimizes fuel and ignition maps for high-octane fuel. It completely transforms throttle response, removes the top speed limiter, and raises the rev limit. It is exceptionally safe for the robust M62 block. Depending on the exact year, it requires physical EPROM chip replacement or early OBD flashing.", zeroToHundred: "6.5s", hundredToTwoHundred: "N/A" },
          { stage: "Stage 2 (Full Exhaust & Cold Air Intake)", power: "320 - 335 hp", notes: "Requires custom exhaust work, removing the highly restrictive factory catalytic converters and resonators, and installing a high-flow intake. This provides a legendary, thunderous V8 roar. However, extracting massive naturally aspirated horsepower from the M62 is financially inefficient.", zeroToHundred: "6.2s", hundredToTwoHundred: "N/A" },
          { stage: "Stage 3 (Centrifugal Supercharger)", power: "420 - 450 hp", notes: "The M62 handles supercharging exceptionally well. Kits from companies like VF Engineering utilize a centrifugal supercharger (like a Vortech V3). The incredibly strong forged connecting rods and Alusil block handle 8-10 PSI of boost with absolute reliability, transforming the heavy E31 into a genuine autobahn missile.", zeroToHundred: "5.0s", hundredToTwoHundred: "N/A" }
        ],
